**Proposition 18.4 (no geometry-only uniform precision cap).** For any
fixed finite cap $C_0\ge0$, no AD policy capped at $p\le C_0$
robustly recovers all $h\in\mathcal H_A$, even allowing arbitrary
adaptive finite controls and later growth.

Proof. On alpha choose $q\ge0$ with $q+1\ge C_0$. The histories
$K^q,K^{q+1}$ have different Time and field difference
$2^{-(q+1)}\le2^{-C_0}$. On a common continuation, Add cancels from
the difference, Reset kills it, Tick contracts it, and raw growth zero
extends it without increasing its norm. Geometry, guards and all
fixed replies agree. Each capped Read has intersecting adjacent
integer report pairs by Lemma 9.1's floor argument. Choosing a common
legal report at every Read gives a complete common adaptive record.
A common finite stop is wrong for one history, and nontermination
violates robust pointwise finiteness. The proof fixes any random tape
for the pathwise version. This is a cap obstruction for this source
and task, not a per-run lower optimum or a physical impossibility.
$\square$

